# The Potato commit this pack is known to be correct against.
#
# Half of this repository's content is generated from Potato's registries and
# checked against them: the three generated references, twelve pinned counts,
# ~140 identifiers named in prose, and the worked-example config, which is a
# byte-for-byte mirror of examples/advanced/full-study-skeleton/config.yaml.
#
# Resolving Potato at its default branch made every one of those a moving
# target. Five of six CI failures in the last sixty runs were that and nothing
# else: "SKILL.md claims 408 documented sub keys, but the registry has 402" and
# "the config.yaml block in worked-example.md has drifted" -- both true of
# Potato-then and false of Potato-now, on commits that were correct when pushed.
#
# So push and pull_request builds resolve this ref, and the weekly cron floats
# to the default branch instead. The cron failing is the signal this file is
# stale; a push failing is now about the push.
#
# To move it: update the SHA, run `python scripts/generate_references.py`,
# `pytest`, and commit the regenerated files together with this change.
